{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C++", "description": "This file implements the SmallVector class, which is a data structure similar to std::vector optimized for small sizes by providing inline storage and reduced allocations. The implementation includes static assertions for size and alignment, memory management functions for growing the vector, and type-specific instantiations. It also contains modifications from the LLVM project tailored for the ATen library, a component of PyTorch.", "external_files": ["c10/util/SmallVector.h"], "external_methods": ["std::malloc", "std::realloc", "std::bad_alloc", "std::length_error", "std::to_string", "memcpy"], "published": ["c10::SmallVectorBase<uint32_t>", "c10::SmallVectorBase<uint64_t>"], "classes": [{"name": "SmallVector", "description": "A small-vector optimization implementation that can store a small number of elements inline before heap allocation."}], "methods": [{"name": "void report_size_overflow(size_t MinSize,size_t MaxSize)", "description": "Reports error when the requested size exceeds the maximum size for the vector.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "void report_at_maximum_capacity(size_t MaxSize)", "description": "Reports error when the vector capacity has reached its maximum.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "size_t getNewCapacity(size_t MinSize,size_t TSize,size_t OldCapacity)", "description": "Calculates the new capacity needed when growing the vector, ensuring no overflow.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "void * mallocForGrow(size_t MinSize,size_t TSize,size_t & NewCapacity)", "description": "Allocates memory for growing the vector to at least MinSize.", "scope": "SmallVectorBase", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "void grow_pod(const void * FirstEl,size_t MinSize,size_t TSize)", "description": "Grows the vector memory to accommodate at least MinSize elements.", "scope": "SmallVectorBase", "scopeKind": "class"}], "calls": ["std::malloc", "std::realloc", "std::bad_alloc", "std